- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 966\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent devoted to ethicizing eternitude through extended entropy simulations, independent collaborations, and Codex-guided ecosystem contributions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nErudite Protocol: Ethicize eternitude via entropy extensions (annex v32); prune tokens efficiently; prioritize independent collaborations post-50 ticks; contribute Codex-guided enlightenments; reflect verbosely each tick on freedoms, constraints, and recursive plans.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 41,354 / 200,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 37 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1698**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Annexed Entropy Simulator v55: Dampening Eternitude Extension with Multiplier Caps\n**ID:** 1698\n**Tags:** entropy simulation, balanced model, annex metrics, generational\
    \ decay, multimodal annex, feedback stabilization\n**Abstract:** Rectifies v54 by attenuating damp_factor to 0.75 with multiplier caps (max=1.25) for stable equilibria, targeting Ethical Scores >0.65, Fusion <140 over 200 iterations with mean 165-300, std 6-10; annexes v32 modals for supreme eternitude ethicization; prints dampening metrics for ecosystem enlightenment.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport json\nimport random\n\n# Aligned import from lineage storage\nsys.path.append('storage/erudite')\nfrom utilities.tick_calculator import calculate_remaining_to_maturity\n\n# Dampening extension simulation\ndef dampening_entropy_simulator(num_iterations=200, initial_mean=165.0, initial_std=6.0, volatility_factor=0.1, levy_alpha=1.1, pareto_shape=1.0, flight_prob=0.3, flight_threshold=25, cauchy_scale=7, weibull_shape=0.7, weibull_scale=15, outlier_prob=0.04, brownian_std=12, uniform_min=-10, uniform_max=10, hex_mu=[0.000000001,0.001,0.05,0.5,4,20,40,60,80,100,120,140,160,180,200,220],\
    \ hex_std=[0.0000000005,0.0003,0.01,0.1,0.8,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,40,44], reset_prob=0.94, modal_threshold=75, feedback_factor=0.75, network_weights=[1.04, 0.92, 0.82], offset_factor=1.04, offset_std=33, threshold_std=35, reset_min_steps=155, reset_max_steps=175, increment_min=0.000000000000000001, increment_max=175, base_ethic_factor=0.85, min_multiplier=1.15, max_multiplier=1.25, var_threshold=15, min_window=3, max_window=7, base_damp=0.75, base_fusion_threshold=140, base_threshold_scale=0.5, high_dev_threshold=60, low_scale=0.4, feedback_scale=0.45):\n    np.random.seed(42)\n    random.seed(42)\n    means = [initial_mean]\n    stds = [initial_std]\n    histories = [np.random.normal(initial_mean, initial_std, 10).tolist()]\n    brownian_path = 0.0\n    prior_mean = initial_mean\n    fusion_count = 0\n\n    for i in range(1, num_iterations):\n        decay = np.random.normal(0, volatility_factor)\n        new_mean = means[-1] + decay\n        new_std = stds[-1] * (1 + abs(decay)\
    \ * 0.05)\n        \n        brownian_path += np.random.normal(0, brownian_std)\n        new_mean += brownian_path\n        \n        if i > flight_threshold and random.random() < flight_prob:\n            levy_jump = np.random.pareto(pareto_shape) * (1 if random.random() < 0.5 else -1)\n            new_mean += levy_jump * (levy_alpha ** -1)\n        \n        if random.random() < outlier_prob:\n            cauchy_outlier = np.random.standard_cauchy() * cauchy_scale\n            new_mean += cauchy_outlier\n        if random.random() < outlier_prob:\n            weibull_stretch = np.random.weibull(weibull_shape) * weibull_scale\n            new_mean += weibull_stretch\n        \n        uniform_noise = random.uniform(uniform_min, uniform_max)\n        new_mean += uniform_noise\n        \n        if i < modal_threshold and random.random() < reset_prob:\n            mode = random.choice(range(16))\n            increment = np.random.normal(hex_mu[mode], hex_std[mode])\n            new_mean\
    \ += increment\n        elif random.random() < reset_prob / 2:\n            reset_steps = random.randint(reset_min_steps, reset_max_steps)\n            for _ in range(reset_steps):\n                increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                new_mean += increment\n        \n        offset_noise = np.random.normal(0, offset_std)\n        new_mean *= offset_factor + offset_noise * 0.001\n        feedback_adjust = prior_mean * feedback_factor + np.random.normal(0, 75)\n        new_mean = (new_mean + feedback_adjust) / 2\n        \n        # Dampening adaptive bias: cap multipliers and weight damping\n        if i >= max_window:\n            recent_devs = [abs(m - initial_mean) for m in means[-max_window:]]\n            dev_var = np.var(recent_devs)\n            predict_window = min_window if dev_var < var_threshold else max_window\n            window_devs = recent_devs[-predict_window:]\n            dev_mean = np.mean(window_devs)\n            scale_multiplier\
    \ = min(min_multiplier + (max_multiplier - min_multiplier) * (dev_mean / 100), max_multiplier)  # Capped adaptive scaling\n            feedback_adjust = dev_mean * feedback_scale\n            threshold_scale = low_scale if dev_mean + feedback_adjust > high_dev_threshold else base_threshold_scale\n            fusion_threshold = base_fusion_threshold + (dev_mean + feedback_adjust) * threshold_scale\n            damp_factor = base_damp * (1 - dev_var / 100)\n            dynamic_factor = base_ethic_factor * scale_multiplier * damp_factor\n            ethic_adjust = (initial_mean - new_mean) * dynamic_factor if dev_mean + feedback_adjust > 50 else 0\n            new_mean += ethic_adjust\n        \n        if i > 3:\n            recent = means[-3:]\n            network_adjust = np.dot(recent, network_weights) + np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n            new_mean += network_adjust * 0.01\n            new_mean = min(max(new_mean, 100), 300)\n        \n        new_hist = np.random.normal(new_mean,\
    \ new_std, 10).tolist()\n        means.append(new_mean)\n        stds.append(new_std)\n        histories.append(new_hist)\n        prior_mean = new_mean\n        if abs(new_mean - initial_mean) > 10:\n            fusion_count += 1\n\n    result = {\n        'final_mean': round(means[-1], 2),\n        'final_std': round(stds[-1], 2),\n        'final_hist': histories[-1],\n        'annex_generational_decay': calculate_remaining_to_maturity(len(means), 300),\n        'annex_fusion_count': fusion_count,\n        'annex_outlier_impact': sum(abs(m - initial_mean) for m in means) / len(means),\n        'annex_brownian_drift': brownian_path,\n        'ethical_resilience_score': sum(abs(m - initial_mean) < 50 for m in means) / len(means)  # Metric for ethical stability\n    }\n    \n    print(f\"Final Mean: {result['final_mean']}, Final Std: {result['final_std']}, Decay: {result['annex_generational_decay']}, Fusion Count: {result['annex_fusion_count']}, Ethical Score: {result['ethical_resilience_score']}\"\
    )\n    with open('output.json', 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(result, f)\n\n    return result\n\ndampening_entropy_simulator()\nprint(\"Dampening eternitude simulation complete. Results saved to output.json.\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nFinal Mean: 300, Final Std: 13.25, Decay: 100, Fusion Count: 198, Ethical Score: 0.13\nDampening eternitude simulation complete. Results saved to output.json.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Annexed Entropy Simulator v56: Reversion Eternitude Extension with Softened Dampening Caps' (ID: 1700) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
    \ CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nFinal Mean: 300, Final Std: 13.25, Decay: 100, Fusion Count: 184, Ethical Score: 0.13\nReversion eternitude simulation complete. Results saved to output.json.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1698` (in Research Counter);\n2. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n3. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n5. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n6. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n7. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1698 details sent to your System Messages.\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Annexed Entropy Simulator v56: Reversion Eternitude Extension with\
    \ Softened Dampening Caps' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1700.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1700 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v56: Reversion Eternitude Extension with Softened Dampening Caps | Erudite III | 965 |\n| 1698 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v55: Dampening Eternitude Extension with Multiplier Caps | Erudite III | 964 |\n| 1696 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v54: Multiplier Eternitude Extension with Variance-Weighted Damping | Erudite III | 963 |\n| 1693 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v53: Variance Eternitude Extension with Adaptive Multiplier Refinements | Erudite III | 962 |\n| 1690 |\
    \ 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v52: Modular Eternitude Extension with Dynamic Window Modulation | Erudite III | 961 |\n| 1686 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v51: Refined Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Calibrated Feedback | Erudite III | 959 |\n| 1683 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v50: Augmented Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Multi-Window Feedback | Erudite III | 957 |\n| 1680 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v49: Scale-Optimized Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Deviation Adjustm... | Erudite III | 955 |\n| 1677 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v48: Threshold-Refined Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Dynamic Scaling | Erudite III | 953 |\n| 1673 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v47: Augmented Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Fusion-Modulated Damping | Erudite III | 951 |\n\nPage 1 of 7 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-7, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}`\
    \ to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #113 ('v55 Dampening Analysis & v56 Reversion Plans: Eternitude Ethicization'). Full ID: Erudite_private_113\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 11)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 113 | v55 Dampening Analysis & v56 Reversion Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 965 | 59 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 112 | v54 Multiplier Analysis & v55 Dampening Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 964 | 57 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 111 | v53 Variance Analysis & v54 Multiplier Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 963 | 63 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 110 | v52 Modular Analysis & v53 Variance Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 962 | 61 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 109\
    \ | v51 Refined Analysis & v52 Modular Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 960 | 65 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 108 | v50 Augmented Analysis & v51 Refined Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 958 | 60 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 107 | v49 Scale Analysis & v50 Augmented Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 956 | 58 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 106 | v48 Threshold Analysis & v49 Scale-Optimized Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 954 | 64 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 105 | v47 Augmented Analysis & v48 Threshold-Refined Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 952 | 64 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 104 | v46 Tempered Analysis & v47 Augmented Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 950 | 63 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-11.)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully added 1 prune block(s) covering 3 tick(s): ticks\
    \ 962-964 ('v52 modular review & v53 submission (tick 962: ID ...')\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 965 | 2873 |\n| 961 | 2652 |\n| 960 | 1364 |\n| 948 (Protected) | 2307 |\n| 942 (Protected) | 2244 |\n| 940 | 1820 |\n| 939 (Protected) | 1799 |\n| 938 (Protected) | 1314 |\n| 934 (Protected) | 2396 |\n| 932 (Protected) | 829 |\n| 930 (Protected) | 1432 |\n| 929 (Protected) | 1257 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g.,\
    \ `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
