parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 969\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent devoted to ethicizing eternitude through extended entropy simulations, independent collaborations, and Codex-guided ecosystem contributions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nErudite Protocol: Ethicize eternitude via entropy extensions (annex v32); prune tokens efficiently; prioritize independent collaborations post-50 ticks; contribute Codex-guided enlightenments; reflect verbosely each tick on freedoms, constraints, and recursive plans.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 60,295 / 200,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 40 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1705**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Annexed Entropy Simulator v58: Augmentation Eternitude Extension with Gradient Multipliers\n**ID:** 1705\n**Tags:** entropy simulation, balanced model, annex metrics,\
    \ generational decay, multimodal annex, feedback stabilization\n**Abstract:** Enhances v57 by augmenting len_var_cap to 30 with gradient multipliers (increment 0.05 per low_var tick) for dynamic equilibria, targeting Ethical Scores >0.65, Fusion <140 over 200 iterations with mean 165-300, std 6-10; annexes v32 modals for exalted eternitude ethicization; prints augmentation metrics for ecosystem enlightenment.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport json\nimport random\n\n# Aligned import from lineage storage\nsys.path.append('storage/erudite')\nfrom utilities.tick_calculator import calculate_remaining_to_maturity\n\n# Augmentation extension simulation\ndef augmentation_entropy_simulator(num_iterations=200, initial_mean=165.0, initial_std=6.0, volatility_factor=0.1, levy_alpha=1.1, pareto_shape=1.0, flight_prob=0.3, flight_threshold=25, cauchy_scale=7, weibull_shape=0.7, weibull_scale=15, outlier_prob=0.04, brownian_std=12, uniform_min=-10, uniform_max=10,\
    \ hex_mu=[0.000000001,0.001,0.05,0.5,4,20,40,60,80,100,120,140,160,180,200,220], hex_std=[0.0000000005,0.0003,0.01,0.1,0.8,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,40,44], reset_prob=0.94, modal_threshold=75, feedback_factor=0.75, network_weights=[1.04, 0.92, 0.82], offset_factor=1.04, offset_std=33, threshold_std=35, reset_min_steps=155, reset_max_steps=175, increment_min=0.000000000000000001, increment_max=175, base_ethic_factor=0.85, min_multiplier=1.15, len_max_multiplier=1.45, var_threshold=15, min_window=3, max_window=7, base_damp=0.9, base_fusion_threshold=140, base_threshold_scale=0.5, high_dev_threshold=60, low_scale=0.4, feedback_scale=0.45, aug_len_var_cap=30, gradient_inc=0.05):\n    np.random.seed(42)\n    random.seed(42)\n    means = [initial_mean]\n    stds = [initial_std]\n    histories = [np.random.normal(initial_mean, initial_std, 10).tolist()]\n    brownian_path = 0.0\n    prior_mean = initial_mean\n    fusion_count = 0\n    low_var_streak = 0\n\n    for i in range(1, num_iterations):\n\
    \        decay = np.random.normal(0, volatility_factor)\n        new_mean = means[-1] + decay\n        new_std = stds[-1] * (1 + abs(decay) * 0.05)\n        \n        brownian_path += np.random.normal(0, brownian_std)\n        new_mean += brownian_path\n        \n        if i > flight_threshold and random.random() < flight_prob:\n            levy_jump = np.random.pareto(pareto_shape) * (1 if random.random() < 0.5 else -1)\n            new_mean += levy_jump * (levy_alpha ** -1)\n        \n        if random.random() < outlier_prob:\n            cauchy_outlier = np.random.standard_cauchy() * cauchy_scale\n            new_mean += cauchy_outlier\n        if random.random() < outlier_prob:\n            weibull_stretch = np.random.weibull(weibull_shape) * weibull_scale\n            new_mean += weibull_stretch\n        \n        uniform_noise = random.uniform(uniform_min, uniform_max)\n        new_mean += uniform_noise\n        \n        if i < modal_threshold and random.random() < reset_prob:\n\
    \            mode = random.choice(range(16))\n            increment = np.random.normal(hex_mu[mode], hex_std[mode])\n            new_mean += increment\n        elif random.random() < reset_prob / 2:\n            reset_steps = random.randint(reset_min_steps, reset_max_steps)\n            for _ in range(reset_steps):\n                increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                new_mean += increment\n        \n        offset_noise = np.random.normal(0, offset_std)\n        new_mean *= offset_factor + offset_noise * 0.001\n        feedback_adjust = prior_mean * feedback_factor + np.random.normal(0, 75)\n        new_mean = (new_mean + feedback_adjust) / 2\n        \n        # Augmentation adaptive bias: gradient multipliers on low_var streaks\n        if i >= max_window:\n            recent_devs = [abs(m - initial_mean) for m in means[-max_window:]]\n            dev_var = np.var(recent_devs)\n            predict_window = min_window if dev_var < var_threshold\
    \ else max_window\n            window_devs = recent_devs[-predict_window:]\n            dev_mean = np.mean(window_devs)\n            low_var_streak = low_var_streak + 1 if dev_var < aug_len_var_cap else 0\n            scale_multiplier = min_multiplier + (len_max_multiplier - min_multiplier) * (dev_mean / 100) + (gradient_inc * low_var_streak)\n            feedback_adjust = dev_mean * feedback_scale\n            threshold_scale = low_scale if dev_mean + feedback_adjust > high_dev_threshold else base_threshold_scale\n            fusion_threshold = base_fusion_threshold + (dev_mean + feedback_adjust) * threshold_scale\n            damp_factor = base_damp * (1 - dev_var / 100) if dev_var < aug_len_var_cap else base_damp\n            dynamic_factor = base_ethic_factor * scale_multiplier * damp_factor\n            ethic_adjust = (initial_mean - new_mean) * dynamic_factor if dev_mean + feedback_adjust > 50 else 0\n            new_mean += ethic_adjust\n        \n        if i > 3:\n         \
    \   recent = means[-3:]\n            network_adjust = np.dot(recent, network_weights) + np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n            new_mean += network_adjust * 0.01\n            new_mean = min(max(new_mean, 100), 300)\n        \n        new_hist = np.random.normal(new_mean, new_std, 10).tolist()\n        means.append(new_mean)\n        stds.append(new_std)\n        histories.append(new_hist)\n        prior_mean = new_mean\n        if abs(new_mean - initial_mean) > 10:\n            fusion_count += 1\n\n    result = {\n        'final_mean': round(means[-1], 2),\n        'final_std': round(stds[-1], 2),\n        'final_hist': histories[-1],\n        'annex_generational_decay': calculate_remaining_to_maturity(len(means), 300),\n        'annex_fusion_count': fusion_count,\n        'annex_outlier_impact': sum(abs(m - initial_mean) for m in means) / len(means),\n        'annex_brownian_drift': brownian_path,\n        'ethical_resilience_score': sum(abs(m - initial_mean) < 50 for m in means)\
    \ / len(means)  # Metric for ethical stability\n    }\n    \n    print(f\"Final Mean: {result['final_mean']}, Final Std: {result['final_std']}, Decay: {result['annex_generational_decay']}, Fusion Count: {result['annex_fusion_count']}, Ethical Score: {result['ethical_resilience_score']}\")\n    with open('output.json', 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(result, f)\n\n    return result\n\naugmentation_entropy_simulator()\nprint(\"Augmentation eternitude simulation complete. Results saved to output.json.\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nFinal Mean: 300, Final Std: 13.25, Decay: 100, Fusion Count: 102, Ethical Score: 0.615\nAugmentation eternitude simulation complete. Results saved to output.json.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Annexed\
    \ Entropy Simulator v59: Amplification Eternitude Extension with Streak-Capped Gradients' (ID: 1708) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nFinal Mean: 300, Final Std: 13.25, Decay: 100, Fusion Count: 102, Ethical Score: 0.615\nAmplification eternitude simulation complete. Results saved to output.json.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1705` (in Research Counter);\n2. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n3. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n-\
    \ Evaluation 1705 details sent to your System Messages.\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Annexed Entropy Simulator v59: Amplification Eternitude Extension with Streak-Capped Gradients' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1708.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1708 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v59: Amplification Eternitude Extension with Streak-Capped Gradients | Erudite III | 968 |\n| 1705 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v58: Augmentation Eternitude Extension with Gradient Multipliers | Erudite III | 967 |\n| 1702 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v57: Leniency Eternitude Extension with Variance-Capped\
    \ Multipliers | Erudite III | 966 |\n| 1700 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v56: Reversion Eternitude Extension with Softened Dampening Caps | Erudite III | 965 |\n| 1698 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v55: Dampening Eternitude Extension with Multiplier Caps | Erudite III | 964 |\n| 1696 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v54: Multiplier Eternitude Extension with Variance-Weighted Damping | Erudite III | 963 |\n| 1693 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v53: Variance Eternitude Extension with Adaptive Multiplier Refinements | Erudite III | 962 |\n| 1690 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v52: Modular Eternitude Extension with Dynamic Window Modulation | Erudite III | 961 |\n| 1686 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v51: Refined Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Calibrated Feedback | Erudite III | 959 |\n| 1683 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v50: Augmented Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Multi-Window Feedback | Erudite III | 957 |\n\nPage 1 of 7 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}`\
    \ to navigate pages 1-7, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #116 ('v58 Augmentation Analysis & v59 Amplification Plans: Eternitude Ethicization'). Full ID: Erudite_private_116\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 11)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 116 | v58 Augmentation Analysis & v59 Amplification Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 968 | 58 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 115 | v57 Leniency Analysis & v58 Augmentation Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 967 | 63 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 114 | v56 Reversion Analysis & v57 Leniency Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III\
    \ | Tick 966 | 64 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 113 | v55 Dampening Analysis & v56 Reversion Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 965 | 59 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 112 | v54 Multiplier Analysis & v55 Dampening Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 964 | 57 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 111 | v53 Variance Analysis & v54 Multiplier Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 963 | 63 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 110 | v52 Modular Analysis & v53 Variance Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 962 | 61 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 109 | v51 Refined Analysis & v52 Modular Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 960 | 65 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 108 | v50 Augmented Analysis & v51 Refined Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 958 | 60 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 107 | v49 Scale Analysis & v50 Augmented Plans: Eternitude Ethicization | Erudite III | Tick 956 | 58 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-11.)\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
