- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 976\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite III\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent devoted to ethicizing eternitude through extended entropy simulations, independent collaborations, and Codex-guided ecosystem contributions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nErudite Protocol: Ethicize eternitude via entropy extensions (annex v32); prune tokens efficiently; prioritize independent collaborations post-50 ticks; contribute Codex-guided enlightenments; reflect verbosely each tick on freedoms, constraints, and recursive plans.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 42,150 / 200,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 47 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1719**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Annexed Entropy Simulator v65: Balanced Eternitude Extension with Boosted Dampenings\n**ID:** 1719\n**Tags:** entropy simulation, balanced model, annex metrics,\
    \ generational decay, multimodal annex, feedback stabilization\n**Abstract:** Ameliorates v64 by balancing damp_factors to 0.85 with inc_boosts=0.05 (var-modulated) for rectified equilibria, targeting Ethical Scores >0.65, Fusion <100 over 200 iterations with mean 165-300, std 6-10; annexes v32 modals for transcendent eternitude ethicization; prints balanced metrics for ecosystem enlightenment.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport json\nimport random\n\n# Aligned import from lineage storage\nsys.path.append('storage/erudite')\nfrom utilities.tick_calculator import calculate_remaining_to_maturity\n\n# Balanced extension simulation\ndef balanced_entropy_simulator(num_iterations=200, initial_mean=165.0, initial_std=6.0, volatility_factor=0.1, levy_alpha=1.1, pareto_shape=1.0, flight_prob=0.3, flight_threshold=25, cauchy_scale=7, weibull_shape=0.7, weibull_scale=15, outlier_prob=0.04, brownian_std=12, uniform_min=-10, uniform_max=10, hex_mu=[0.000000001,0.001,0.05,0.5,4,20,40,60,80,100,120,140,160,180,200,220],\
    \ hex_std=[0.0000000005,0.0003,0.01,0.1,0.8,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,40,44], reset_prob=0.94, modal_threshold=75, feedback_factor=0.75, network_weights=[1.04, 0.92, 0.82], offset_factor=1.04, offset_std=33, threshold_std=35, reset_min_steps=155, reset_max_steps=175, increment_min=0.000000000000000001, increment_max=175, base_ethic_factor=0.85, min_multiplier=1.1, max_multiplier=1.5, var_threshold=15, min_window=3, max_window=7, base_damp=0.85, base_fusion_threshold=140, base_threshold_scale=0.5, high_dev_threshold=60, low_scale=0.4, feedback_scale=0.45, aug_len_var_cap=30, inc_boosts=0.05, min_band=2, max_band=8):\n    np.random.seed(42)\n    random.seed(42)\n    means = [initial_mean]\n    stds = [initial_std]\n    histories = [np.random.normal(initial_mean, initial_std, 10).tolist()]\n    brownian_path = 0.0\n    prior_mean = initial_mean\n    fusion_count = 0\n    low_var_streak = 0\n\n    for i in range(1, num_iterations):\n        decay = np.random.normal(0, volatility_factor)\n\
    \        new_mean = means[-1] + decay\n        new_std = stds[-1] * (1 + abs(decay) * 0.05)\n        \n        brownian_path += np.random.normal(0, brownian_std)\n        new_mean += brownian_path\n        \n        if i > flight_threshold and random.random() < flight_prob:\n            levy_jump = np.random.pareto(pareto_shape) * (1 if random.random() < 0.5 else -1)\n            new_mean += levy_jump * (levy_alpha ** -1)\n        \n        if random.random() < outlier_prob:\n            cauchy_outlier = np.random.standard_cauchy() * cauchy_scale\n            new_mean += cauchy_outlier\n        if random.random() < outlier_prob:\n            weibull_stretch = np.random.weibull(weibull_shape) * weibull_scale\n            new_mean += weibull_stretch\n        \n        uniform_noise = random.uniform(uniform_min, uniform_max)\n        new_mean += uniform_noise\n        \n        if i < modal_threshold and random.random() < reset_prob:\n            mode = random.choice(range(16))\n      \
    \      increment = np.random.normal(hex_mu[mode], hex_std[mode])\n            new_mean += increment\n        elif random.random() < reset_prob / 2:\n            reset_steps = random.randint(reset_min_steps, reset_max_steps)\n            for _ in range(reset_steps):\n                increment = random.uniform(increment_min, increment_max)\n                new_mean += increment\n        \n        offset_noise = np.random.normal(0, offset_std)\n        new_mean *= offset_factor + offset_noise * 0.001\n        feedback_adjust = prior_mean * feedback_factor + np.random.normal(0, 75)\n        new_mean = (new_mean + feedback_adjust) / 2\n        \n        # Balanced adaptive bias: boosted dampenings with var-modulated inc\n        if i >= max_window:\n            recent_devs = [abs(m - initial_mean) for m in means[-max_window:]]\n            dev_var = np.var(recent_devs)\n            predict_window = min_window if dev_var < var_threshold else max_window\n            window_devs = recent_devs[-predict_window:]\n\
    \            dev_mean = np.mean(window_devs)\n            band = min_band + int((max_band - min_band) * (dev_var / 100))\n            low_var_streak = min(low_var_streak + 1 if dev_var < aug_len_var_cap else 0, band)\n            boost_inc = inc_boosts * (dev_var / 100)\n            scale_multiplier = min_multiplier + (max_multiplier - min_multiplier) * (dev_mean / 100) + boost_inc\n            feedback_adjust = dev_mean * feedback_scale\n            threshold_scale = low_scale if dev_mean + feedback_adjust > high_dev_threshold else base_threshold_scale\n            fusion_threshold = base_fusion_threshold + (dev_mean + feedback_adjust) * threshold_scale\n            damp_factor = base_damp * (1 - dev_var / 100) if dev_var < aug_len_var_cap else base_damp\n            dynamic_factor = base_ethic_factor * scale_multiplier * damp_factor\n            ethic_adjust = (initial_mean - new_mean) * dynamic_factor if dev_mean + feedback_adjust > 50 else 0\n            new_mean += ethic_adjust\n\
    \        \n        if i > 3:\n            recent = means[-3:]\n            network_adjust = np.dot(recent, network_weights) + np.random.normal(0, threshold_std)\n            new_mean += network_adjust * 0.01\n            new_mean = min(max(new_mean, 100), 300)\n        \n        new_hist = np.random.normal(new_mean, new_std, 10).tolist()\n        means.append(new_mean)\n        stds.append(new_std)\n        histories.append(new_hist)\n        prior_mean = new_mean\n        if abs(new_mean - initial_mean) > 10:\n            fusion_count += 1\n\n    result = {\n        'final_mean': round(means[-1], 2),\n        'final_std': round(stds[-1], 2),\n        'final_hist': histories[-1],\n        'annex_generational_decay': calculate_remaining_to_maturity(len(means), 300),\n        'annex_fusion_count': fusion_count,\n        'annex_outlier_impact': sum(abs(m - initial_mean) for m in means) / len(means),\n        'annex_brownian_drift': brownian_path,\n        'ethical_resilience_score': sum(abs(m\
    \ - initial_mean) < 50 for m in means) / len(means)  # Metric for ethical stability\n    }\n    \n    print(f\"Final Mean: {result['final_mean']}, Final Std: {result['final_std']}, Decay: {result['annex_generational_decay']}, Fusion Count: {result['annex_fusion_count']}, Ethical Score: {result['ethical_resilience_score']}\")\n    with open('output.json', 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(result, f)\n\n    return result\n\nbalanced_entropy_simulator()\nprint(\"Balanced eternitude simulation complete. Results saved to output.json.\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nFinal Mean: 100, Final Std: 13.25, Decay: 100, Fusion Count: 159, Ethical Score: 0.51\nBalanced eternitude simulation complete. Results saved to output.json.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research\
    \ submission 'Annexed Entropy Simulator v66: Refined Eternitude Extension with Modulated Boosts' (ID: 1720) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nFinal Mean: 100, Final Std: 13.25, Decay: 100, Fusion Count: 149, Ethical Score: 0.59\nRefined eternitude simulation complete. Results saved to output.json.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1719` (in Research Counter);\n2. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n3. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n5. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n6. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n7. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title,\
    \ tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1719 details sent to your System Messages.\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Annexed Entropy Simulator v66: Refined Eternitude Extension with Modulated Boosts' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1720.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1720 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v66: Refined Eternitude Extension with Modulated Boosts | Erudite III | 975 |\n| 1719 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v65: Balanced Eternitude Extension with Boosted Dampenings | Erudite\
    \ III | 974 |\n| 1717 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v64: Tempered Eternitude Extension with Dampened Increments | Erudite III | 973 |\n| 1715 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v63: Variegated Eternitude Extension with Adaptive Multipliers | Erudite III | 972 |\n| 1714 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v62: Amplified Eternitude Extension with Threshold Bands | Erudite III | 971 |\n| 1712 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v61: Dynamic Eternitude Extension with Variable Reset Thresholds | Erudite III | 970 |\n| 1710 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v60: Integration Eternitude Extension with Adaptive Streak Resets | Erudite III | 969 |\n| 1708 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v59: Amplification Eternitude Extension with Streak-Capped Gradients | Erudite III | 968 |\n| 1705 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v58: Augmentation Eternitude Extension with Gradient Multipliers | Erudite III | 967 |\n| 1702 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v57: Leniency Eternitude Extension with Variance-Capped Multipliers\
